n2a42f40 ard(worker:engineer): #317 Adds the Kubernetes API layer for the executor: minimal JSON types, a `…\nb599337 feat: Kubernetes executor, part 6A: kube REST client, types and… (#317)\n861e89c ard(triage:lead): #349 This is a docs-only change. It rewrites the README, the site's getting-… [skip ci]\nc522dae ard(triage:lead): #394 The request is a clear change: when a job slot is freed, the pool shoul… [skip ci]\na6a6c2b feat: ard init and setup, part C: init writes the local tree, --… (#390)\n5dfd4e1 ard(triage:engineer): #384 Adds a `needs-network` worker status with a strictly validated `network… [skip ci]\n658a412 ard(triage:engineer): #316 Adds the three hidden pod-side commands (pre, exec, post) as separate p… [skip ci]\n2c9c4ed ard(triage:engineer): #317 Plans only the Kubernetes API layer: minimal types, a client interface,… [skip ci]\n3033d6a merger: doc gate 5 reads commit statuses as well as check runs (#393)\n D .ard/317/worker-engineer.md\n?? .ard-input/","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01C1ecp9XahETCqy8758xUHt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
